cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this repository or the TR-WM-EVAL benchmark, please cite both the
  archived release and, once it appears, the paper. Note that the data is not
  uniformly licensed: read DATA_LICENSE.md before reuse.
title: >-
  turkish-llm-watermarking: code and data for TR-WM-EVAL, a Turkish
  watermark-evaluation benchmark
abstract: >-
  Code, corpora, detector scores and LLM-judge annotations behind a study of how
  three watermarking schemes (KGW, EXP, SynthID) behave on Turkish. TR-WM-EVAL
  contains 4,000 human text windows across three registers, 384 generated Turkish
  texts, 3,840 attacked texts across ten removal attacks, 58,161 detector scores
  including a length-controlled rescoring and an eight-key sweep, and 788 pairwise
  judge verdicts. Known limitations are stated up front in BENCHMARK.md. This
  repository is a research fork of MarkLLM and therefore also carries upstream
  files the study does not use; DATA_LICENSE.md itemises them.
type: software
version: 1.6.0-paper
